ament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[3,13,15,16,17]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11,16]}],"places":[{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[1,5]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[5]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[5,6,13]},{"id":"galilee_433","name":"Galilee","kind":"Region","lat":32.70675,"lon":35.30153,"summary":"Circuit. Solomon rewarded Hiram for certain services rendered him by th